     "lng": 10.685,
     "hours": "Mon-Sat 10:00-17:00 Sun 13:00-17:00; The church will be closed for renovation work from 2 November 2026 until expected May 2027",
     "price": "",
     "wikidata": "Q695065",
     "content": "The largest church in Lübeck, and a key example of brick Gothic architecture. Built between 1277 and 1351, it features the highest brick vault in the world.",
     "editions": 29
    },
    {
     "kind": "see",
     "name": "The Dom",
     "lat": 53.8608,
     "lng": 10.6858,
     "hours": "May-Sep Mon-Sat 10:00-18:00 Sun 11:30-16:00 Oct-Apr 10:00-16:00",
     "price": "",
     "wikidata": "Q3916007",
     "content": "Founded in 1173 by Henry the Lion, this is one of the oldest monuments in Lübeck and the first large brick church built on the Baltic coast. Initially constructed as a Romanesque basilica and later converted into a Gothic hall church, it is",
     "editions": 24
