     "lng": 10.6833,
     "hours": "11:00-16:00",
     "price": "",
     "wikidata": "Q896458",
     "content": "Its tower platform (which can be reached by an elevator) offers a great view over the city, and if weather conditions allow it you can even see Travemünde (17&nbsp;km to the north-east).",
     "editions": 13
    },
    {
     "kind": "see",
     "name": "St. Jakobi",
     "lat": 53.8709,
     "lng": 10.689,
     "hours": "Core hours 10:00-15:00 (varies by season)",
     "price": "",
     "wikidata": "Q375042",
     "content": "This 14th-century seafarers' church survived World War II intact, preserving its original historic interior. It is known for its historic pipe organs and a memorial chapel dedicated to the lost sailing ship ''Pamir''.",
     "editions": 12
    },
    {
     "kind": "see",
     "name": "St. Aegidien",
     "lat": 53.8639,
     "lng": 10.6898,
     "hours": "Tue-Sat 10:00-16:00",
     "price": "",
     "wikidata": "Q316973",
     "content": "The smallest of Lübeck's five medieval parish churches was spared from destruction in World War II. Its interior combines medieval frescoes with a carved 1587 Renaissance singers' gallery and a prominent Baroque altar.",
     "editions": 6
    },
    {
     "kind": "see",
